{"name":"Winterberry Frost","hex":"#b4474d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winterberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of holly native to the United States and Canada and producing red berries, Ilex verticillata.","The fruit of this plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winterberry"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ilex verticillata","blocks":[{"text":"Ilex verticillata, the winterberry, is a species of holly native to eastern North America in the United States and southeast Canada, from Newfoundland west to Ontario and Minnesota, and south to Alabama."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Ilex_verticillata_fruits_and_foliage_1.JPG/330px-Ilex_verticillata_fruits_and_foliage_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilex_verticillata"},{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330px-Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"htt